Spec: Route progress

Purpose:
  Where a position lies on a reference route: distance along, distance left, offset, off-route and finish.

Owns:
  ./route_progress.dart
  /test/domain/route_progress_test.dart

References:
  /docs/specs/history/17-follow-route.md
  /docs/specs/history/18-follow-reverse.md

Must:
  Off route means more than `30` m from the route.
  The finish counts within `30` m of the last point once at least `90` % of the route is behind the rider.
  The first fix takes the first pass of the route through the position, so a loop start never reads as its finish.
  While on route only the next `500` m are searched and progress never decreases.
  After being off route the pass nearest the previous progress is taken; ties go to the pass ahead.
  A reference with fewer than two points gives no progress.

Scenario: loop start
  Given a loop whose start and finish are the same place
  When the first fix is at the start
  Then the finish is not reached
